WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.100
Ready?

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.740
The US celebrated record high
school graduation rates five times in

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:14.370
the past five years. But test scores have
been flat, raising red flags about grad

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:18.240
rate inflation. Of course, schools offer
supports to students at risk of not

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.810
graduating. Chief among them: Credit
recovery, makeup classes that give

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:25.140
failing students a second chance to
graduate on time. While widespread,

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:29.609
participation is uneven. 39 percent of
all students taking credit recovery

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:34.649
attend just 8% of high schools. At that
volume, schools create a quality problem

00:00:34.649 --> 00:00:39.420
where second chances become inferior
second tracks to graduation. But these

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:43.829
schools also have far more poor and
minority students, making this quality

00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:48.719
problem an equity problem. Despite much
lower test scores and grad rates, these

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:53.789
peak credit recovery schools have the
highest graduation rate gains, bolstering

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:58.440
fears that lowered expectations will
leave many graduates unprepared. Done

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:02.969
well, credit recovery gives students
second chances. Done poorly, it offers our

00:01:02.969 --> 00:01:07.920
least advantaged a second track that can
harm students and schools.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.320
To learn more about my take on credit recovery, check out the link in the description below.

